  {
   "evidence_id": "EV_001",
   "speaker_id": "",
   "speaker_role": "",
   "transcript_text": "It's cramping pain in the lower tummy. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. Is there anything that triggers it? It's worse with stress and certain foods. I've had alternating constipation and loose stools too, for about three months. Oh, and bloating. That's been about the same, six months. Let me check your vitals now. Almost there... Okay: heart rate 84, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, BP is 118 over 81, respiratory rate 18. Come over here and I'll have a look. Tell me if anything hurts. Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses. Alright, and what about night-time diarrhoea, anaemia, fever or blood in the stool? No night-time diarrhoea, anaemia, fever or blood in the stool, none of it. Is your urine normal, no changes? Hmm, no, that's all fine. Any procedures or operations? I had a knee arthroscopy three years ago. I did try to ignore it for a while. Any allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? No allergies. Any relatives with health problems I should be aware of? My father had kidney stones. Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? Right, it's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. Since when have you been taking it? Two months now. And alcohol, how much? I don't drink at all. Do you work? I run a small shop, so I'm on my feet a lot. And what do you usually eat? Mostly home-cooked food, rice and vegetables. Are you active at all? Barely, I'm mostly sedentary these days. Any long-term health problems I should know about? I have anxiety, for nearly five years. Having listened and examined, this is probably irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. Another possibility is coeliac disease.",
